<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leo Africanus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1510</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leo Africanus was a Moroccan-born traveller and writer who visited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> in the early sixteenth century. His description of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, later published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, was for centuries a key European source on the region. He described <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timbuktu">Timbuktu</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> around 1510 as a wealthy city where books were among the most profitable goods traded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leo-africanus.jpg" alt="Leo Africanus" width="309" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sebastiano del Piombo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sebastiano_del_Piombo_Portrait_of_a_Humanist.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
